Package: bridgenorm
Title: Cytometry Batch Correction from Bridge Samples
Version: 0.9.0
Authors@R:
    person("M. D.", "Manurung", email = "m.d.manurung@lumc.nl", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Estimates technical batch effects in cytometry data from bridge
    samples, reference material from the same donor measured in every batch.
    Cells are assigned to the nodes of a self-organising map, a paired shift
    is fitted per batch and node, and each batch's marker quantiles are then
    mapped onto those of an anchor batch within each node, shrinking small
    nodes toward the batch-wide curve. A paired-shift baseline is included.
    Study samples never enter a fit. Models are frozen with a digest and
    applied to new data without changing earlier corrections. Formerly 'heb'.
